WEBVTT

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.230
Yo, you look like you haven't slept much.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.550
Tsuchiura-kun!

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.460
Do you always come this early?

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.120
No, I just was thinking of practicing a bit before class started.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.660
And you've been staying in the practice rooms late after school recently, haven't you?

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.730
Yeah...

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.380
Kanayan would say: "She doesn't have anything else to do!"

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.370
That's just too mean!

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:10.060
Irreplaceable Melody

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:17.060
All I can do right now is practice, after all.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:22.150
So that I live on without a guilty conscious after taking second place in the competition.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.020
The midterm exams will begin next week. Make sure to study properly for them.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.470
Understood, Hino-san?

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:31.830
Yes!

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.260
Practice Room Reservation Schedule

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.370
They're all full, as I figured.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.220
Um, you're Hino-sempai from General Studies, right?

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:44.780
Yes.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.680
Would you like me to switch out for you?

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.520
I'm the one who reserved room 204, Kawamura.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.590
But...

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.040
Your Canon for the second selection was wonderful! Please do your best!

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.650
Thank you.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:04.480
If I don't practice more and more, I'll betray all the people who are cheering me on as well.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.330
And for the magical violin itself as well, I must...

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:12.570
Lili.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.000
What are you doing?

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.220
I'm going to keep this violin for a little while.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:19.500
Maintenance again?

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.750
No, this is different.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.300
Then, why?

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.240
It's almost time for midterms.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.000
Having a passion for practicing is good and all, but you can't neglect your studies.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.570
Huh?

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:35.560
Give it back! I have to keep practicing.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.630
It doesn't look like you've been sleeping much lately. You shouldn't push yourself so hard.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:44.060
And I can't have it be my fault that your grades have started to slip.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.110
So that's that. Make sure to study properly!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.570
Lili!

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:59.020
And I had finally decided to really practice as much as I could...

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:09.440
It's not good to practice so single-mindedly, Kahoko Hino.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.800
For you, or for that violin.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.610
You're going to take a break from practicing for a while?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.880
Yeah, since the exams are soon.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:25.750
I see. You haven't studied one bit, have you, Kaho?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.780
Exactly.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:30.420
Don't worry! We haven't started studying for the exam either.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.750
Let's study together.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.750
Sure.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.630
Without my violin, I have no reason to go to the Music Department, do I?

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:48.740
I made curry yesterday, you know!

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:54.890
I've just returned to my life before I entered the competition, but still...

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:02.010
Why does it that I feel like something's missing?

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.070
Hino-chan!

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.860
What are you spacing out about?

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:10.290
I was going to study for my exams while listening to a CD,

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.550
but I just couldn't concentrate for some reason.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.290
Are you still practicing even with exams coming up?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.350
I'm actually stuck with studying for exams as well.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:24.690
But at times like this I just play my trumpet and blast on through!

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.550
It was just like this when I started playing the trumpet, wasn't it?

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.240
When was that?

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:36.790
During my first year in middle school, you see...

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.200
Who's there?

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.500
I'm Kazuki Hihara, First Year, Class 2, number 10 on the track and field team.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.430
This is a trumpet. You knew that, right?

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.330
So, why are you here everyday anyway?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:38.290
S-Sorry! Just, while I was eating lunch, I figured... Am I in your way?

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.500
You're not in my way, no...

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:43.880
Hihara-kun, here.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.870
I borrowed it from the club room.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.130
If you're so interested, why not try playing it first?

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.360
Cool!

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.850
Here, try and play it.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:09.180
Back then it felt really great, and was fun.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.080
I can never forget that feeling, even today.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.610
I think I understand somehow.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:23.020
I also cannot forget the first time I heard Ave Maria, and how it reverberated in my heart.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.440
Kaho-sempai.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:30.930
Fuyuumi-chan!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.310
Are you going to go practice now?

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:36.080
Yes. If I don't practice every day I get unsure of myself.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.060
I see.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.560
What about you, Kaho-sempai?

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.650
I'm studying for exams.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:44.440
You have college entrance exams next year. That sounds tough, Sempai.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.130
Yeah.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.860
Everyone in the Music Department practices every day.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.660
At this rate I'll fall further and further behind!

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.690
Too bad, there. Can't even solve such a simple problem?

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.580
Ts-Tsuchiura-kun.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.210
You need to substitute that equation in here.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.390
Now figure the rest out yourself.

00:08:07.390 --> 00:08:09.150
Huh?

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.090
At least finish telling me how to solve it!

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.130
If I did that, what's the point?

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.770
Do your best.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:16.850
Sure...

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:17.720
See you.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.130
Sheesh...

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.030
What?

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:24.190
That was a nice mood you had there.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:28.510
I'm so jealous! You're surrounded by so many wonderful people, Kaho-chan!

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:35.030
It's all thanks to playing the violin that I know everyone.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:39.520
Violin expanded my world for me.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:47.810
Buying study guides right before exams? I'm just so pitiful...

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.440
A violin?

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.480
What am I...

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.250
What was that just now?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.580
Some kind of street performer or something?

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:37.910
I started it just because Lili begged me at first.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:42.060
But then, why do I want to play the violin so much?

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.900
It's over!

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.890
Kaho, how'd you do?

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.020
Please don't ask me about it.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.660
That's right! I have to go to the music classrooms!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.570
Something irreplaceable?

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.920
Right. That's the theme of the third selection.

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:17.600
It's another high-minded abstract concept for the third selection...

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.090
You've got to expand your image, man.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.710
Doesn't sound too convincing when Kanayan says it.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:25.470
You got that right!

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.860
Oh, be quiet.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:31.440
Yunoki! What is something irreplaceable to you?

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.220
Me?

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:34.780
Yes, that's it...

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:39.430
People's kindness, perhaps?

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.890
Is something the matter, Hino-san?

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:45.030
Are you OK?

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:46.910
I'm fine.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.880
You scary bastard.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:52.600
Well, everyone has something different that's irreplaceable.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.750
Make sure to think hard about it.

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:58.850
Something irreplaceable to me?

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.540
Um, Kaho-sempai...

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.330
What is it, Fuyuumi-chan?

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:16.830
About the piece for the competition... I can just never decide on one.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:18.910
I'm the same way.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:24.080
If you don't mind, could I ask you about which piece would be good for me to choose?

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.370
OK then, let's think about it together.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.640
Aren't you two being a bit naive?

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:31.020
Amo-san.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.580
You're rivals when it comes to the competition.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.250
Rivals?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:42.090
That's right! And anyway, there's no point performing it if you didn't pick out the piece yourself.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.600
I guess that's true.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.650
Fuyuumi-chan, let's both think about it and do our best.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:50.520
OK.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:55.360
Lili, Lili, come out!

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:00.260
Hey, you're there, aren't you? Stop playing with me and come out!

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:04.880
Sheesh, why won't he come out?

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:09.720
They announced the theme, and I have to practice at least a little!

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:13.000
I've got to get much better!

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.580
Kahoko Hino...

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:20.380
I can't give the violin back to you as you are right now.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.330
Why wouldn't Lili come out, I wonder?

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:35.480
Oh, Hino. What's wrong?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.610
Kanazawa-sensei.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.550
Don't let your guard down just because midterms are over.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.990
The third selection is almost here.

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:47.790
Ah man, I totally sounded like a teacher just then.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.710
Well anyway, keep thinking hard about what's irreplaceable to you.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:57.750
I know! So, if you'll excuse me.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.210
Hino-san!

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:22.130
Yes?

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.670
Excuse me, I'm Sugita, from the library.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:33.770
This notebook was left in the library, and I think it's either Tsukimori-kun's or Tsuchiura-kun's.

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.370
Do you know who it is?

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:37.540
R.T.?

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:41.210
"Ren Tsukimori" or "Ryotaro Tsuchiura?"

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.030
Both of them are R.T.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:46.400
Both of them were in the library before.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.470
Oh, Tsukimori-kun, perfect timing!

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:51.750
Is this yours, Tsukimori-kun?

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:58.480
No, it's not. I spell my name with an "L", not an "R."

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.210
This is mine.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.490
What's with the "L?"

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.930
It's personal preference.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:10.850
And if I were as careless to forget my notes, I wouldn't be nitpicking others.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.650
You see everything that way, don't you?

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:17.920
Even when you perform everything just stands on ceremony, with this cold, aloof feeling.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:22.420
And you... Don't you let your emotions get in the way?

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.420
What did you say?

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.940
H-Hey now, you two!

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.780
Sorry, just got a little hot headed there.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.000
Sorry about that. Thanks for returning my notes.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:35.960
No problem.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:42.070
We ended up going from notes to talking about playing styles.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:48.900
Both you and Tsuchiura-kun really think about music all the time, everyday, don't you?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:53.570
Your performance also has problems with its style, etc...

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.240
Try looking in a mirror more.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.080
Is my hair messed up from this morning?

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:03.070
No. The form of your left arm supporting the violin needs work.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:06.840
You bend your elbow out too far and your wrist sticks out too much.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:11.340
You should look in a mirror and check that you are holding it properly.

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:17.060
Thank you.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.020
I'm home!

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:22.650
Kahoko, perfect timing.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.770
What is it?

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:26.610
I'd like you to bring something to your sister that she forgot.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.690
Here, thanks a lot.

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:33.530
Here.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:35.600
Thank you! Sorry about this.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:36.830
Sheesh...

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:55.760
Oh, so these are the instruments that developed into the violin.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.180
Fractional violins?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.470
You can choose the size based on your own height.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:02.770
Ah, cute!

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:07.450
So the bow is strung with horse hair?

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.840
You didn't know?

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.880
Shimizu-kun?

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:15.630
I see you came too, Sempai.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:21.290
Yeah. You'll come out to things like this Shimizu-kun, huh?

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:28.300
Yes. I think I should know as much as I can about the instrument to give a good performance.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:37.760
Stuck on the back of a violin there is a part called a brace.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:41.980
Along with reinforcing the face board,

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.980
it also serves to amplify and strengthen the bass notes.

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:54.630
The structure of the cello and the violin are mostly the same.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:17:02.080
But in order to produce deeper sounds the body is larger and thicker.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:09.550
There are many different stringed instruments in the Orient as well.

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:16.290
The koto or the biwa are strung with silk string.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:19.150
Shimizu-kun, you really know a lot.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:24.230
Even though I've been playing it, I don't really know much at all about the violin.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:29.440
But, Sempai, you seemed entranced.

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:32.120
You think?

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.030
Yes.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:40.540
You really love playing the violin, don't you, Sempai?

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:43.520
I love the... violin?

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:50.210
Yes. It's really just that simple. I love the violin.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.280
Yes, I do!

00:17:55.820 --> 00:18:02.140
Thanks a lot for today. I really learned a lot because you were there, Shimizu-kun.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:05.630
Sorry for taking so much of your time.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:07.400
No...

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:14.780
Lately I've been really interested in you, Sempai.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:22.240
For some reason, your performance is fascinating.

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:25.200
Oh, you meant my performance.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:36.170
Why is it? Why does your sound remain stuck in my ears?

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:39.690
Well, if you'll excuse me.

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:41.080
Yeah, until next time.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:49.430
It seems like everyone who is participating in the competition is connected through music.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:53.550
Whether we get along or not, or like each other or not,

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.700
we're all connected through music.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.620
Hey, Lili! Come out!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.960
I want to play the violin!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:14.300
It's not for the competition, or because I want to get better...

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:18.400
It's that I love the violin! That's why I want to play!

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:21.800
Please return the violin to me!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.180
Lili!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:29.810
Kahoko Hino, I've been waiting for you to say those words.

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:34.070
I wanted you to play the violin with those honest feelings.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:35.130
Here!

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:47.790
I'm also glad that you've come to love the violin so much.

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:52.500
I can finally play again!

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:56.620
I'd like you to never forget this feeling.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:00.550
Right now the thing that's irreplaceable for me...

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:04.070
The piece that taught that to me...

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:50.020
Th-These grades are just too sad...

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:54.710
Even after taking a break from practicing, this is the best grade I could get?

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:59.770
Hey, Hino-san, what's the matter?

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:02.030
You were sighing.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.550
Y-Yunoki-sempai?

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:07.870
Oh, my, those are pretty poor marks there.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:11.410
I hate dummies, you know.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:15.290
It's not like I care about what other people think, really!

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:19.830
Anyway, won't you move?

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:20.920
Why?

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:26.430
Because, if someone sees this, won't that be a problem for you, Yunoki-sempai?

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:29.660
Do you think I'd be that careless?

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.180
Not really.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:31.890
Right?

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:36.760
So is this fun for you, then, huh?

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.440
Oh, be quiet, you.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.010
Won't you let me play with you?

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.390
Just kidding, just kidding.

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:49.830
You're such a blockhead.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:52.790
This guy's just...

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:58.000
I just can't get enough of you, Kahoko.

00:21:58.730 --> 00:22:00.800
Kahoko?

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:04.070
Why is he suddenly calling me by my first name?

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:39.730
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:42.550
The cello is one of the violin family,

00:23:42.550 --> 00:23:47.940
however instead of holding it under your chin to play, you stand it between your legs.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:52.420
And for that purpose there's a special pole called an End Pin.

00:23:52.420 --> 00:23:54.100
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:59.110
The cello can cover a large range of notes from very low to very high,

00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:02.490
so what instrument is it called the closest to?

00:24:02.490 --> 00:24:05.060
The answer will come at the end of the program!

00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:08.090
Oh, no! Hino-chan is engaged!

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:09.630
Huh? For real?

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.140
Engaged... Engaged...

00:24:13.370 --> 00:24:16.140
Next episode: Capriccio for a Young Girl's Heart.

00:24:17.020 --> 00:24:19.230
Why am I here?

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:24.040
The answer is... The Human Voice!
